export anchor SleeperTrainStyle:
    number: 416
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Sleeper train
    idea: A night train compartment, walnut panelling and brass trim around a rounded window that holds the route as lit towns along a railway, a printed timetable card with dotted leaders for the itinerary, and small punched ticket cards on a brass rack.
    base: dark
    palette:
        night: #120c08, the page edge and the style sheet
        walnut: #2a1a10, the panelled compartment wall with a faint vertical grain
        card: #1e1510, the timetable card, ticket cards and list rows
        line: #4a3424, row rules, double rules and card edges
        brass: #d9b26a, the window frame, rack, corner clips, dates and the primary button
        onBrass: #22160a, text on brass
        cream: #f3e6cc, text and town names
        muted: #c4b08f, italic captions and details
        lamp: #ffd98a, lit towns and focus
        booked: #9fd99a, Booked and punched rows
        unbooked: #f2a27a, Not booked and To do
    type:
        Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Georgia. Base 16px at
        1.5. The timetable title 38px at 400, card titles 22px, stops 18px
        at 600, details 15px italic, labels 15px small caps tracked 0.18em
        in brass, dates with old style tabular numbers.
    layout:
        The whole screen sits on a walnut wall with a faint vertical grain.
        A pill brass edged plate runs across the top with a ringed B crest
        and Brightwork Trips in small caps, and Night service with the dates
        in italic on the right. Below, two columns. On the left a rounded
        window in a thick brass frame shows a night view, stars, a crescent
        moon, dark hills and a brass railway linking three lit towns
        labelled Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka, with an italic caption under it.
        Under the window a card holds the conductor's weather note, a 52px
        17 degrees beside the text and a pink blossom line. On the right the
        timetable card has brass corner clips. It reads Timetable for over
        Japan in April and the party in italic, then six rows each with the
        date in brass, the stop in bold with a dotted leader, the detail in
        italic below and a small caps status at the right. Two buttons close
        the card. A rounded brass rack bar spans the width, and under it two
        ticket cards. Ticket checks shows each item with a punched round
        hole when done or a dashed square when not. Fare purse shows euro
        3,200 saved of 5,000 with a brass rail and a cream marker at 64
        percent. Below 960px all columns stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 28px between window and timetable, 24px between ticket cards and 12px timetable rows.
    density: Medium. A full timetable of six rows beside one large window.
    corners: A 36px brass window frame round a 26px glass, a 40px pill plate, 6px cards and 4px buttons.
    borders: 1px dark wood edges, double rules under headings, dotted leaders from stop to detail and brass corner clips on the timetable.
    shadows: Warm deep drops under the window, the cards and the brass rack.
    icons:
        Thin 1.5 stroke icons. Booked is a check circle, Not booked a dashed
        circle and Flight a plane. A done check is a punched round hole and
        a To do check a dashed square.
    focus: A 2px lamp yellow outline offset 3px with a faint warm halo.
    tone: Old railway courtesy such as Timetable for, Ticket checks, Fare purse and Conductor's weather note.
